      "quality": "poor",
      "qualityReason": "editorial_filler"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Tonalea sits along U.S. Route 160, also known as the Navajo Trail, a historic corridor across the Southwest.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        5,
        6
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tonalea%2C_Arizona",
      "category": "transport",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "Historically, Tonalea was also called Red Lake, reflecting the area's natural water features.",
